From 564d7d1705567d1010cc49c31a3ca96f69d47fb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Himess <semihcvlk53@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:20:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(kms-worker): E3, the KDA route, in the connector
 (lifecycle Level 3)

The kms-worker takes the E3 route (rules K4-K6) in front of Profile H on
the RFC-016 path, when `profile_h.kda_schemes` names at least one FIPS 204
parameter set. A request whose signature field is
abi.encode(signerBytes, sig) and whose requester is the key-derived
address is verified natively; a failure is refused for good, with no
ECDSA or ERC-1271 fallback. Any other request goes through Profile H as
before. The delegation itself is the usual delegated V1 check with the
KDA as delegate, so retirement and revocation apply unchanged.

`profile_h.kda_k8_mode` selects how the node runs ML-DSA (K8):
`single:<impl>` or `agree:<impl>,<impl>`; a disagreement is refused and
logged. The worker logs the signature check's wall time with each
verdict (`sig_check_us`), for the latency measurement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
